{"resultsPerPage":13,"startIndex":0,"totalResults":13,"format":"NVD_CVE","version":"2.0","timestamp":"2026-11-24T09:27:41.566","vulnerabilities":[{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-121745","sourceIdentifier":"7ffcee3d-2c14-4c3e-b844-86c6a321a158","published":"2026-11-04T22:17:53.970","lastModified":"2026-11-10T21:46:30.450","vulnStatus":"Awaiting Analysis","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"Node Version Manager (nvm) is a POSIX-compliant shell function for managing multiple node.js versions. In versions 0.40.0 through 0.40.8, when `NVM_AUTH_HEADER` is set, `nvm_download` passes the credential to curl or wget as a `--header \"Authorization: ...\"` command-line argument. Process arguments are visible to every local user (on Linux via `ps` or `/proc//cmdline` unless `/proc` is mounted with `hidepid=`; on macOS via `ps`), so another unprivileged account on the same machine can read the token while nvm is downloading during `nvm ls-remote`, `nvm install`, and similar commands, and gain whatever access it grants on the private mirror. Only users who set `NVM_AUTH_HEADER` on a host shared with other local accounts are affected. Version 0.41.0 passes the header to curl on stdin and to GNU Wget in a private temporary config file. BusyBox wget reads no config file, so when it is the only downloader available the header is still passed as an argument."}],"affected":[{"source":"7ffcee3d-2c14-4c3e-b844-86c6a321a158","affectedData":[{"vendor":"nvm-sh","product":"nvm","defaultStatus":"unaffected","repo":"https://github.com/nvm-sh/nvm","versions":[{"version":"0.40.0","lessThan":"0.41.0","versionType":"semver","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV40":[{"source":"7ffcee3d-2c14-4c3e-b844-86c6a321a158","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"4.0","vectorString":"CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","baseScore":2.0,"baseSeverity":"L